TidyHeap Director (THD) is a sample application that is actually a tool that is shipped in a built state with TidyHeap (and ACS). We thought it would be a useful sample app in that it shows a rather simplistic but useful use of a TFileBasedDocument.The files that THD can modify are the settings files manipulated by TidyHeap - titled 'YOUR APP.prf". If you change the settings using THD, TidyHeap will read in and use the settings when running your app so that you can change the debugging behavior of TidyHeap with recompiling and linking your application. THD director must be able to read in and write out the settings files. The TFileBasedDocument portion of THD handles the document becoming dirty and will automatically manages the setting file for you while the document is open. The most complicated part of the TDocumentTidyHeap is managing the many bools in the format of the settings file. It is critical that the data be read in and out in the same order (obviously ;-). This is the most error prone portion of the document.